---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Privacy Policy · Lovepins" description="How Lovepins handles your data: what we collect, why, who processes it, and how to delete it." path="/privacy">
<article class="prose wrap">
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated: November 23, 2026</p>
  <p>Lovepins is a private map for couples. This policy explains what we collect, why, who processes it for us, and how to delete it. The short version: we keep only what the app needs to sync your shared map between your two phones. No ads, no tracking, no selling of data.</p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Why</th><th>Where it lives</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Email address</td><td>To sign you in: the address you register with a password, or the one provided by Apple (Sign in with Apple, possibly a private relay address) or Google (Sign in with Google).</td><td>Our servers (Supabase)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Apple or Google user identifier</td><td>If you use Sign in with Apple or Sign in with Google, to recognize your account.</td><td>Our servers (Supabase)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Password</td><td>If you sign up with email and password, to sign you in. It is stored only as a one-way hash; we can never read it.</td><td>Our servers (Supabase)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>First name</td><td>Shown to your partner in the app.</td><td>Our servers</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Profile photo (optional)</td><td>Shown to your partner in the app. Resized to a small square before upload.</td><td>Our servers (Supabase Storage, private)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Your couple</td><td>Who you are paired with, your invite code, and the date you got together (optional).</td><td>Our servers</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Pins</td><td>Title, date, position on the map (latitude/longitude), rating, notes, memory or wishlist, and who added it. Shared with your partner only.</td><td>Our servers</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Subscription status</td><td>To unlock Lovepins Premium for both partners. Purchases are handled by Apple; we receive the subscription status linked to an anonymous couple identifier, never your payment details.</td><td>RevenueCat, Apple</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Technical logs</td><td>Our hosting provider keeps short-lived request logs (such as IP address and time) for security and debugging.</td><td>Supabase</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>What stays on your iPhone</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Photos</strong> you add to a pin are stored only on the iPhone that added them. They are not uploaded to our servers, so your partner does not see them.</li>
    <li><strong>Your profile photo</strong>, if you add one, is the exception: it is resized to a small square and stored on our servers (Supabase Storage) so your partner can see it. Only you and your partner can access it. Removing it or deleting your account deletes the file.</li>
    <li><strong>Your location</strong> is used on your device to center the map and find date ideas nearby. We never send or store your location on our servers. To find places, the app uses Apple Maps search, which Apple processes under <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">its own privacy policy</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Reminders</strong> (anniversaries, "one year ago today") are local notifications scheduled on your iPhone.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>What we don't do</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>No advertising, no ad identifiers, no tracking across apps or websites.</li>
    <li>No third-party analytics.</li>
    <li>We never sell or rent your data.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="waitlist">Our website and the launch waitlist</h2>
  <p>This website (lovepins.app) sets no cookies and uses no analytics or tracking.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Waitlist.</strong> If you join the waitlist, we store your email address (and the time you signed up) on our servers (Supabase). We use it for one thing only: to email you once when Lovepins is available on the App Store. We never share it, never add you to a newsletter, and delete the whole list after that email. To be removed earlier, email <a href="mailto:hello@lovepins.app">hello@lovepins.app</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Abuse protection.</strong> To stop bots from flooding the form, we keep a one-way hash of your IP address for 24 hours. The address itself is never stored.</li>
    <li><strong>Hosting.</strong> The website is hosted by Cloudflare, which keeps short-lived request logs for security.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who processes data for us</h2>
  <p>We use a small number of service providers, only to run the app:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Supabase</strong> (database, sign-in, real-time sync), hosted in the United States (AWS us-east-1).</li>
    <li><strong>Google</strong>, for Sign in with Google (only if you choose it), under <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">its own privacy policy</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>, to host this website and route emails sent to hello@lovepins.app.</li>
    <li><strong>RevenueCat</strong>, to manage subscription status across your two phones.</li>
    <li><strong>Apple</strong>, for Sign in with Apple, App Store payments, maps and place search.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Each provider processes data on our behalf and under its own security and privacy commitments.</p>

  <h2>Who can see your data</h2>
  <p>Your pins, your first name and your couple's start date are visible only to you and your partner. Access is enforced on our database for every request. We access data only when needed to operate the service or when you ask us for help.</p>

  <h2>Retention</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your data is kept while your account exists.</li>
    <li>When you delete a pin, it disappears from both phones right away. It is kept on our servers in deleted form so the deletion syncs to your partner's phone, and it is erased with your couple's data.</li>
    <li><strong>If you leave your couple</strong>, the pins you added stay on the map you shared with your partner. Your app starts fresh and the data stored on your iPhone for that couple is erased.</li>
    <li><strong>If you delete your account</strong>, your account, email address and first name are deleted from our servers. If your partner is still in the couple, the shared pins stay on their map without your name. If you were alone, your couple and all its pins are deleted.</li>
    <li>Short-lived technical logs are deleted automatically by our hosting provider.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Deleting your account</h2>
  <p>In the app: open the <em>Us</em> tab → <em>Delete my account</em>. Deletion is immediate and permanent. If you signed in with Apple, we also revoke Lovepins' access to your Apple ID. Deleting your account does not cancel an App Store subscription: manage it in Settings › Apple ID › Subscriptions.</p>
  <p>You can also email us at <a href="mailto:hello@lovepins.app">hello@lovepins.app</a> to request access to, correction of, or deletion of your data.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>Lovepins is not intended for children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect data from them.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If we change this policy, we will update this page and the date above. Significant changes will be announced in the app.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about privacy: <a href="mailto:hello@lovepins.app">hello@lovepins.app</a></p>

  
</article>
</Layout>
